>>
endobj
445 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 105 0 R
/E (The Automatic Railway Level Crossing Controller was successfully designed and implemented using Verilog Hardware Description Language. The controller uses a finite state machine to coordinate train detection, gate operation, warning indication, and road traffic signals. It also incorporates a warning counter and fault-detection logic to handle selected invalid sensor conditions.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
446 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 105 0 R
/E (Functional verification was performed using Synopsys VCS, and the resulting signal waveforms were analyzed using GTKWave. The simulation exercised the normal crossing sequence, including train approach, warning, gate closing, train passage, gate opening, and return to the idle state. A selected invalid gate-sensor combination was also applied to evaluate the fault-handling behavior.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
447 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 105 0 R
/E (Code coverage analysis was performed using line, toggle, condition, branch, and FSM coverage metrics. The results showed 89.32% line coverage, 80.56% toggle coverage, 63.64% condition coverage, 75.86% branch coverage, and 42.86% FSM coverage. These results demonstrate that the testbench exercised several important parts of the design while also identifying opportunities for additional verification.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
448 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 105 0 R
/E (The RTL design was subsequently synthesized using Synopsys Design Compiler with the configured SAED32 standard-cell library. The synthesis process generated a technology-mapped netlist, a schematic representation, and reports for quality of results, area, timing, and power.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
449 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 105 0 R
/E (Overall, the project demonstrates an RTL-to-synthesis workflow for an FSM-based digital control system. It provides practical experience in Verilog design, simulation, waveform analysis, coverage evaluation, timing constraints, and logic synthesis. Further verification and confirmation of the numerical synthesis results would strengthen the assessment of the implementation.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
